    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3586" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argūmentōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Rich in proof</i> (v. argumentum, I. A.),
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 9</span></i>; Acron. ad <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				3, 70</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Rich in matter</i> or <i>material</i>
			(v. argumentum, II. A. a.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 5, 10, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
